      "source": [
        "# Hybrid mechanistic and machine learning ensemble\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook runs the bioreactor project and creates the submission CSV files.\n",
        "\n",
        "Use Python 3.11 or newer. Python 3.12 is a good choice for this package.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Step 1. Find the project and choose the mode\n",
        "\n",
        "Leave `MODE = \"regenerate\"` for the quick run. This uses the saved predictions for the supplied challenge data and creates the CSV files again.\n",
        "\n",
        "Change the same setting to `MODE = \"retrain\"` only when you want to fit the models again. Training can take a long time. It uses the original modeling and validation recipe, including the validation limitations discussed in the guide. Its recorded error is not a confirmed leaderboard result.\n",
        "\n",
        "For local Jupyter, extract the ZIP and open this notebook inside the `bioreactor_ready_to_run` folder. In Google Colab, open this notebook and upload `bioreactor_ready_to_run.zip` when the next cell asks for it.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the cells in order. The notebook generates files without submitting them to the leaderboard.\n"
      ]
    },
